<div class="lens-concrete-example provenance-example" role="group" aria-labelledby="{{EXAMPLE_PREFIX}}-title">
<p class="lens-overline">{{PROVENANCE_ICON}}<span>Provenance in the incident</span></p><h3 id="{{EXAMPLE_PREFIX}}-title">Follow the missing-record claim back to its sources</h3>
<p class="incident-flow-intro">For ticket {{CASE_TICKET_ID}}, follow the comparison permitted by the authority records: its saved inputs, method, recorded observation and the assessment it supports.</p>
<ol class="incident-flow" role="list" aria-label="From incident sources to a bounded assessment">
<li><span class="incident-flow-number" aria-hidden="true">01</span><div class="incident-flow-content"><h4>Identify the two inputs</h4><span class="incident-flow-record">Source records · exact versions and file digests</span><dl class="incident-flow-sources"><div><dt>Required set · {{CASE_SNAPSHOT}}</dt><dd><strong>{{CASE_REQUIRED_COUNT}} identifiers</strong><span>{{CASE_ACCOUNT}} · <code>{{CASE_FILTERS}}</code></span></dd></div><div><dt>Saved output · {{CASE_OUTPUT}}</dt><dd><strong>{{CASE_OUTPUT_ROW_COUNT}} exported rows</strong><span>Run {{CASE_RUN}} · service revision {{CASE_SERVICE_REVISION}}</span></dd></div></dl></div></li>
<li><span class="incident-flow-number" aria-hidden="true">02</span><div class="incident-flow-content"><h4>Compare the actual row identifiers</h4><span class="incident-flow-record">Comparison method · version {{CASE_METHOD_VERSION}}</span><p>The method identifies which required identifiers are absent from {{CASE_OUTPUT}}. Comparing the counts alone would not establish which rows are missing.</p><p class="incident-flow-result">{{CASE_MISSING_COUNT}} required identifiers are absent.</p></div></li>
<li><span class="incident-flow-number" aria-hidden="true">03</span><div class="incident-flow-content"><h4>Save what was observed and how</h4><span class="incident-flow-record">Operational Observation · version {{CASE_OBSERVATION_VERSION}}</span><p>The agent in investigation session {{CASE_SESSION}} records the missing identifiers, exact sources, method execution and limitations. Export run {{CASE_RUN}} and investigation session {{CASE_SESSION}} are separate records.</p></div></li>
<li><span class="incident-flow-number" aria-hidden="true">04</span><div class="incident-flow-content"><h4>Use the evidence for a bounded assessment</h4><span class="incident-flow-record">Evidence Set supports Failure Assessment</span><p>An Evidence Set preserves the sources and comparison for this claim, including counterevidence and gaps. It supports the assessment that output {{CASE_OUTPUT}} is incomplete under definition {{CASE_DEFINITION_VERSION}} for this account, filters and snapshot.</p></div></li>
</ol>
<div class="incident-flow-boundary"><strong>The omission is established within this scope.</strong><p>Cause, affected downstream uses, other accounts and recovery still need investigation. The service owner remains responsible for the assessment and incident response.</p></div>
<details class="incident-flow-details"><summary>Inspect the formal result and provenance fields</summary>
<div class="example-formal-result"><code>R = RequiredIds({{CASE_SNAPSHOT}}, {{CASE_ACCOUNT}}, { {{CASE_FILTERS}} })</code><code>M = R ∖ ExportedIds({{CASE_OUTPUT}})</code><code>|R| = {{CASE_REQUIRED_COUNT}}; |M| = {{CASE_MISSING_COUNT}} ⇒ ¬Complete({{CASE_OUTPUT}}, {{CASE_SNAPSHOT}}, {{CASE_ACCOUNT}}, { {{CASE_FILTERS}} })</code></div>
<dl class="incident-flow-field-map"><div><dt>Subject · x</dt><dd>The exact Operational Observation version {{CASE_OBSERVATION_VERSION}}.</dd></div><div><dt>Sources · sourceᵢ</dt><dd>The Source records identifying snapshot {{CASE_SNAPSHOT}} and saved output {{CASE_OUTPUT}}.</dd></div><div><dt>Relationships · relationᵢ</dt><dd>The observation <em>originates from</em> each Source record, with the origin role declared as required input or observed output.</dd></div><div><dt>Operation · operationᵢ</dt><dd>Method {{CASE_METHOD_VERSION}}’s identifier comparison, execution record and limitations.</dd></div><div><dt>Recorder and owner · ownerᵢ</dt><dd>Agent session {{CASE_SESSION}} records the observation; the service owner retains responsibility for the assessment and response.</dd></div><div><dt>Standing · postureᵢ</dt><dd>Inputs are recorded sources. Definition {{CASE_DEFINITION_VERSION}} has its own owner acceptance. The observation records a datum; the assessment remains candidate review material.</dd></div></dl>
<p>A separate Finding, when recorded, derives from the Evidence Set and preserves the same support and limits. This trail records how the information was produced; any permission to act comes from the applicable authority records.</p>
</details>
</div>
